  "sourceFetchedAt": "2026-10-28T00:52:45.138086+00:00",
  "bodyHtml": "\n\n\t\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-byline\">\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-author\"><a href=\"/archive/source-37895d34f8cef391272c/\" rel=\"author\" class=\"url fn n\"><span>pwsbuilder</span></a></span>\n\t\t\t\t<time class=\"entry-published updated\" datetime=\"2018-04-04T20:12:16-04:00\" title=\"Wednesday, April 4, 2018, 8:12 pm\">April 4, 2018</time>\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"comments-link\"></span>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-content\">\n\t\t\t<p>Guild of Harwich Artists Meeting, April 21, 2018, 2:00p.m., Harwich Community Center, <a href=\"https://maps.google.com/?q=100+Oak+Street,+Harwich&amp;entry=gmail&amp;source=g\">100 Oak Street, Harwich</a></p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_3691\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img class=\"size-large wp-image-3691\" src=\"/media/archive/d17255b1dfa0aac5f04facefc3d173ee67601596fa2738e94c66fefb8f3133b6.jpg\" alt=\"©Andrew Kusmin, Blind Faith\" width=\"1024\" height=\"636\" loading=\"lazy\" /><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-3691\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">©Andrew Kusmin, Blind Faith</figcaption></figure>\n<figure id=\"attachment_3689\" class=\"wp-caption alignright\"><img class=\"wp-image-3689 size-full\" src=\"/media/archive/8a2db9ccb9d9328f0a456205f21bd30adaea0a34ba1c8f1dfb9a9613ea8f6d51.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" loading=\"lazy\" /><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-3689\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Andrew Kusmin</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The Guild of Harwich Artists welcomes watercolor artist, Andrew Kusmin, at its meeting on Saturday, April 21 at 2:00p.m.  He will provide a presentation he’s been sharing across New England. It centers on not just his art but his journey to becoming an artist. He brings and shares many, many paintings – his own and some created by his mentors – and encourages his audience to consider the importance not just of how and what to paint but <em>WHY</em> to paint. The program is based around his recent book, “Palette of Dreams.”</p>\n<p>Kusmin’s work has been exhibited nationwide by:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The National Watercolor Society</li>\n<li>The American Watercolor Society</li>\n<li>Watercolor Art Society–Houston</li>\n<li>Salmagundi Club National</li>\n<li>Knickerbocker Arts National and</li>\n<li>The New England Watercolor Society</li>\n</ul>\n<figure id=\"attachment_3690\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img class=\"size-large wp-image-3690\" src=\"/media/archive/aee0dcf40285e673ca5568f298d8cb9c7f070f8db08de2b14b3fcb72da4a4166.jpg\" alt=\"©Andrew Kusmin, A Time For Iris\" width=\"719\" height=\"1024\" loading=\"lazy\" /><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-3690\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">©Andrew Kusmin, A Time For Iris</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Most Recent Awards:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2015 Gold Medal, New England Watercolor Society</li>\n<li>First in Watercolor, Plymouth Annual Open</li>\n<li>2016 Guild of Boston Artists Award for Excellence in Realism</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<footer class=\"entry-footer\">\n\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-terms category\">Posted in <a href=\"/archive/source-24848e4ea0af8641d360/\" rel=\"tag\">EDUCATION</a>, <a href=\"/archive/source-74004cd9be5de0d40a61/\" rel=\"tag\">EVENTS</a>, <a href=\"/archive/source-f25f8a22f42584a0f3e3/\" rel=\"tag\">MONTHLY MEETINGS</a>, <a href=\"/archive/source-e23b79be08a822c7b682/\" rel=\"tag\">WHAT'S NEW</a></span>\t\t\t<br /><span class=\"entry-terms post_tag\">Tagged <a href=\"/archive/source-f4e998c8f6939a763b08/\" rel=\"tag\">Andrew Kusmin</a>, <a href=\"/archive/source-c5a0664c0f5b2d29d271/\" rel=\"tag\">Guild of Harwich Artists</a>, <a href=\"/archive/source-8287b39eda106d181640/\" rel=\"tag\">Monthly Meetings</a></span>\t\t</footer>\n\n\t\n",
